      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will update the commit message tomorrow, but in short, USB device may have multiple configurations (https://www.beyondlogic.org/usbnutshell/usb5.shtml#ConfigurationDescriptors), but setting different configuration will disturb other users of this device. Even more, Linux documentation discourage using USBDEVFS_SETCONFIGURATION (https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/driver-api/usb/usb.html#synchronous-i-o-support). Because of that I think that fastboot should use only active USB configuration to avoid implementing logic for switching configurations.\nAt the moment fastboot can find interface X at configuration 1 and claim it, even if the device\u0027s active configuration is Y and interface X at configuration Y is something completely different (e.g. has only one endpoint).",
